<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barwick-in-Elmet</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barwick-in-Elmet is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-yorkshire">West Yorkshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, east of Leeds. It keeps large earthworks of an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort, later reused for a Norman motte, and its name recalls the British kingdom of Elmet, which survived in the area until the early 7th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barwick-in-elmet.jpg" alt="Barwick-in-Elmet" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chemical Engineer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barwick_Maypole_cross_pubs_14_June_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
